{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7f1c0de-0000-4000-8000-5f7a9b1c2d00",
    "name": "STX REST API (/api/v1)",
    "description": "The STX exchange REST API.\n\nEvery route requires an Ed25519 signature - there are no public REST endpoints. Postman's script sandbox has no Ed25519 implementation, so the signature cannot be computed here: set the `timestamp` and `signature` collection variables per request with the openssl one-liner in postman/README.md, or use ./verify, javascript/rest/quickstart.mjs or python/rest/quickstart.py, which sign for you.\n\nPrices are integer cents throughout. A market's ceiling is its own max_price (100 on a US $1 market, 10000 on a Canadian $100 market), not a fixed 99.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "https://demo.stxapp.io",
      "description": "US integration. Canada integration is https://api-staging.on.sportsxapp.com; Canada production is https://api.on.stxapp.ca."
    },
    {
      "key": "key_id",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Your API key id. Not a secret."
    },
    {
      "key": "timestamp",
      "value": "",
      "description": "Unix MILLISECONDS, as a string. Must be within 30s of the server clock."
    },
    {
      "key": "signature",
      "value": "",
      "description": "base64 Ed25519 signature of timestamp + METHOD + path. Regenerate per request."
    },
    {
      "key": "market_id",
      "value": "",
      "description": "A market UUID from GET /api/v1/markets."
    },
    {
      "key": "order_id",
      "value": "",
      "description": "An order UUID from POST or GET /api/v1/orders."
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Identity",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Get the authenticated account",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-KEY",
                "value": "{{key_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-TIMESTAMP",
                "value": "{{timestamp}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-SIGNATURE",
                "value": "{{signature}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/me",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "me"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns {\"me\": {...}} - user_id, account_id, key_id, scope. This is the only place your user_id is published, and private WebSocket topics (active_orders:<user_id>) need it.\n\nSign this request before sending it. The signed message is timestamp_ms + METHOD + path, where path includes the query string exactly as sent. See postman/README.md for the one-liner that fills in {{timestamp}} and {{signature}}."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Markets",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List markets",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-KEY",
                "value": "{{key_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-TIMESTAMP",
                "value": "{{timestamp}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-SIGNATURE",
                "value": "{{signature}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/markets?status=open&limit=50",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "markets"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "open"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "50"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns {cursor, markets: [...]}. Pass the cursor back as ?cursor=... for the next page; it is null on the last page.\n\nKnown issue: ?status=open also returns suspended markets, and trading=true is ignored as a query param. Filter on the `trading` field client-side.\n\nSign this request before sending it. The signed message is timestamp_ms + METHOD + path, where path includes the query string exactly as sent. See postman/README.md for the one-liner that fills in {{timestamp}} and {{signature}}."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List events",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-KEY",
                "value": "{{key_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-TIMESTAMP",
                "value": "{{timestamp}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-SIGNATURE",
                "value": "{{signature}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/events",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "events"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns {cursor, events: [...]}.\n\nSign this request before sending it. The signed message is timestamp_ms + METHOD + path, where path includes the query string exactly as sent. See postman/README.md for the one-liner that fills in {{timestamp}} and {{signature}}."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Orders",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Place an order",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-KEY",
                "value": "{{key_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-TIMESTAMP",
                "value": "{{timestamp}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-SIGNATURE",
                "value": "{{signature}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/orders",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "orders"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns 200 (not 201) as {\"order\": {...}}.\n\nThe body is FLAT: wrapping it in {\"user_order\": {...}}, the way the GraphQL mutation takes it, returns 400.\n\n`price` is a whole number of cents, strictly below the market's max_price. A rejection reports the cap in DOLLARS while the field is CENTS: price 4650 on a $1 market returns 422 \"The order's price must be lower than 1.00\".\n\nNeeds a read_write key.\n\nSign this request before sending it. The signed message is timestamp_ms + METHOD + path, where path includes the query string exactly as sent. See postman/README.md for the one-liner that fills in {{timestamp}} and {{signature}}.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"market_id\": \"{{market_id}}\",\n  \"order_type\": \"limit\",\n  \"action\": \"buy\",\n  \"price\": 42,\n  \"quantity\": 5,\n  \"client_order_id\": \"postman-1\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "List orders",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-KEY",
                "value": "{{key_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-TIMESTAMP",
                "value": "{{timestamp}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-SIGNATURE",
                "value": "{{signature}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/orders?status=open&limit=50",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "orders"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "open"
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "50"
                }
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns {cursor, orders: [...]}, most recent first. Filters: order_ids, client_order_ids, market_ids, status - all comma-separated.\n\nSign this request before sending it. The signed message is timestamp_ms + METHOD + path, where path includes the query string exactly as sent. See postman/README.md for the one-liner that fills in {{timestamp}} and {{signature}}."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Get an order",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-KEY",
