            },
            "description": "Returns {\"order\": {...}}, or 404 for an id that is not yours.\n\nSign this request before sending it. The signed message is timestamp_ms + METHOD + path, where path includes the query string exactly as sent. See postman/README.md for the one-liner that fills in {{timestamp}} and {{signature}}."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Cancel an order",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-KEY",
                "value": "{{key_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-TIMESTAMP",
                "value": "{{timestamp}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-SIGNATURE",
                "value": "{{signature}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/orders/{{order_id}}",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "orders",
                "{{order_id}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns {order_id, status, next_geolocation_at}.\n\nA cancel is a request, not a guarantee: a fill already in flight can still land afterwards.\n\nNeeds a read_write key.\n\nSign this request before sending it. The signed message is timestamp_ms + METHOD + path, where path includes the query string exactly as sent. See postman/README.md for the one-liner that fills in {{timestamp}} and {{signature}}."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Cancel several orders",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-KEY",
                "value": "{{key_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-TIMESTAMP",
                "value": "{{timestamp}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-SIGNATURE",
                "value": "{{signature}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/orders/batched",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "orders",
                "batched"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns {cancellations: [{order_id, status}]}. Each entry of the request is an OBJECT carrying an order_id, not a bare id string. An unknown id comes back with status \"Order not found\" rather than failing the call.\n\nNeeds a read_write key.\n\nSign this request before sending it. The signed message is timestamp_ms + METHOD + path, where path includes the query string exactly as sent. See postman/README.md for the one-liner that fills in {{timestamp}} and {{signature}}.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"orders\": [\n    {\n      \"order_id\": \"{{order_id}}\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Cancel all open orders",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-KEY",
                "value": "{{key_id}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-TIMESTAMP",
                "value": "{{timestamp}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-STX-ACCESS-SIGNATURE",
                "value": "{{signature}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/orders/all",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
